From oliver.heid at siemens.com  Thu Mar 20 11:06:13 2008
From: oliver.heid at siemens.com (Heid, Oliver)
Date: Thu, 20 Mar 2008 12:06:13 +0100
Subject: SRM keyboard problem
Message-ID: <E3E4FC5CDA935240BCD2A8AE47B98DD472944F@ERLM862A.ww001.siemens.net>

Update: Got the graphical console back to work. Since the srm manual is a bit short here: The trick (obviously) is to remove the keyboard, mouse and - essential ! - also the VGA cable, set "console" to serial (via rs232), power cycle, set "console" back to graphics (via rs232), power off again, connect keyboard, mouse and video, power on, and voila!
I seem to have booted the machine once with either vga or keyboard unplugged.
    Oliver

